The key word is Alchemy.

You wanted to know? Here we go...

First I want to mention that I just use a single (of more possible)
recipes...

1. make your potion of healing stack as large as possible (by ID'ing
   and/or B/U/C IDing and/or diluting the potions a *single* level
   if necessary)[*]
2. dip a stack of potions of healing into a potion of speed
3. restack as in 1. all potions of extra healing
4. dip a stack of all the potions of extra healing into a potion of
   gain level
5. restack as in 1. all potions of full healing
6. bless the resulting stack of potions of full healing

Use only non-cursed potions for alchemy.

Occasionally some potions may explode. (Don't worry about that.)

A stack of, e.g., 15 blessed diluted potions of full healing will
provide 120 HPs.

[*] Important emphasis: Diluting a stack of diluted potions will turn
    them to water. Careful!

